content.p:
DfE carefully considered and applied the Dransfield

 Dransfield v. IC and anor; Craven v IC and anor [2015] EWCA Civ 454
		     criteria for an "objective standard" of vexatiousness and found that the Requests had no reasonable foundation in terms of the sought information being of value (to the requester, public or section of the public) due to previous responses and correspondence from DfE;

Parker

 Colin Parker v IC [2016] UKUT (AAC)
		     stated that the public interest in the requested information cannot act as a "trump card" against a finding of vexatiousness;
